# The look of {{APP_NAME}}

This folder holds the app's theme: its colours, fonts and corner radius, chosen when the app was
requested in the portal. The platform wrote it once, when it created the repository. From now on
it is the app's own code: changing the theme in the portal later changes nothing here.

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `theme.css` | the theme as CSS variables on `:root`: `--brand-primary`, `--brand-on-primary`, `--brand-background`, `--brand-surface`, `--brand-text`, `--brand-muted-text`, `--brand-border`, `--brand-accent`, `--brand-font`, `--brand-heading-font`, `--brand-radius` |
| `theme.json` | the same values as data (`id`, `name`, `description`, `logoUrl` when the theme has a logo, `tokens`), for code that can't read CSS, such as PDF or e-mail templates and charts |

## How the app uses it

- **Node.js starter:** `src/client/main.tsx` imports `theme.css`, and `src/client/styles.css`
  styles the pages with the variables. Without this folder the app falls back to a neutral look.
- **Other stacks:** when the app gets pages, serve `theme.css` with the app's own static files
  and link it before the app's own stylesheet.

Use the variables for every colour, font and radius (`color: var(--brand-text)`), never
hard-coded values. The AI agent's `ui-and-brand` skill has the rules: contrast, accessibility,
the logo.

## Own brand: replace the placeholders

If `theme.json` has `"placeholder": true`, the app asked for its own brand and the values are
placeholders (a built-in theme of the platform). Replace them in **both** files with your brand's
colours, fonts and corner radius, then delete `"placeholder": true` and the `PLACEHOLDERS`
comment at the top of `theme.css`.

- Text must stay readable: at least 4.5:1 contrast between text and its background (WCAG AA),
  for `--brand-text` on `--brand-background` and `--brand-surface`, and for
  `--brand-on-primary` on `--brand-primary`.
- Fonts: fonts installed on users' devices, or font files kept in this repository if their
  licence allows it. Never fonts loaded from another website.
- Logo: keep the file in the repository and serve it from the app; the app's security settings
  block images from other websites.

## Changing the look

Edit `theme.css` and `theme.json` together so they keep the same values, and note the change in
`CHANGELOG.md`.
